#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:22
msgid "Quantum Sampling for Energy-Based Models"
msgstr "Quantum Sampling for Energy-Based Models"

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:33
msgid ""
"[Why Quantum? Revisiting the Sampling "
"Bottleneck](quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md): The intractable partition "
"function, slow MCMC mixing, and the quantum alternative."
msgstr ""
"[Why Quantum? Revisiting the Sampling "
"Bottleneck](quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md): The intractable partition "
"function, slow MCMC mixing, and the quantum alternative."

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:34
msgid ""
"[Simulated Annealing for Ising Models](simulated_annealing.md): Mapping "
"energy functions to Ising Hamiltonians and building a local sampling "
"baseline."
msgstr ""
"[Simulated Annealing for Ising Models](simulated_annealing.md): Mapping "
"energy functions to Ising Hamiltonians and building a local sampling "
"baseline."

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:35
msgid ""
"[Integrating Quantum Samplers into PyTorch](quantum_sampling_pytorch.md):"
" Swapping the local SA sampler for the CIM sampler within the KPP "
"training loop, with the core interfaces explained."
msgstr ""
"[Integrating Quantum Samplers into PyTorch](quantum_sampling_pytorch.md):"
" Swapping the local SA sampler for the CIM sampler within the KPP "
"training loop, with the core interfaces explained."

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:37
msgid "Tutorial 1: Generative Modeling with a Full Boltzmann Machine"
msgstr "Tutorial 1: Generative Modeling with a Full Boltzmann Machine"

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:46
msgid ""
"[BM Generation](bm_generation.md): Unsupervised data generation with a "
"fully connected Boltzmann Machine. Example: `example/bm_generation/`."
msgstr ""
"[BM Generation](bm_generation.md): Unsupervised data generation with a "
"fully connected Boltzmann Machine. Example: `example/bm_generation/`."

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:48
msgid "Tutorial 2: Feature Learning and Classification with RBMs and DBNs"
msgstr "Tutorial 2: Feature Learning and Classification with RBMs and DBNs"

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:58
msgid ""
"[RBM Classification: Handwritten Digit "
"Recognition](rbm_classification.md): Feature learning and classification "
"with a single RBM. Example: `example/rbm_digits/rbm_digits.ipynb`."
msgstr ""
"[RBM Classification: Handwritten Digit "
"Recognition](rbm_classification.md): Feature learning and classification "
"with a single RBM. Example: `example/rbm_digits/rbm_digits.ipynb`."

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:59
msgid ""
"[DBN Classification: Deep Belief Networks](dbn_classification.md): "
"Stacking RBMs into a Deep Belief Network for hierarchical features. "
"Example: `example/dbn_digits/supervised_dbn_digits.ipynb`."
msgstr ""
"[DBN Classification: Deep Belief Networks](dbn_classification.md): "
"Stacking RBMs into a Deep Belief Network for hierarchical features. "
"Example: `example/dbn_digits/supervised_dbn_digits.ipynb`."

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:61
msgid "Tutorial 3: Quantum Variational Autoencoder (Q-VAE)"
msgstr "Tutorial 3: Quantum Variational Autoencoder (Q-VAE)"

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:70
msgid ""
"[Q-VAE: Quantum Variational Autoencoder](qvae_mnist.md): Replacing the "
"Gaussian prior with a quantum RBM for image generation and representation"
" learning. Example: `example/qvae_mnist/run_pipeline.py`."
msgstr ""
"[Q-VAE: Quantum Variational Autoencoder](qvae_mnist.md): Replacing the "
"Gaussian prior with a quantum RBM for image generation and representation"
" learning. Example: `example/qvae_mnist/run_pipeline.py`."

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:72
msgid "Case Studies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:74
msgid ""
"Case studies build directly on the hands-on tutorials and show how KPP is"
" used on larger-scale public datasets. Each study packages a complete "
"pipeline — data loading, model definition, training, and evaluation — and"
" lives alongside a runnable example under `example/`. Pages marked "
"*Coming soon* will be expanded in follow-up PRs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:85
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[Q-VAE for Single-Cell Transcriptomics](qvae_cell.md) *Coming soon*: "
"single-cell representation learning with a QVAE; UMAP and clustering "
"evaluation (Leiden, classification, scIB, scGraph, DPT). Example: "
"`example/qvae_cell/`."
msgstr ""
"**Q-VAE for Single-Cell Transcriptomics**: single-cell representation "
"learning with a QVAE: expression matrix → low-dimensional representations"
" → UMAP → clustering evaluation. Example: "
"`example/qvae_cell/train_qvae_cell.ipynb`."

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/index.md:86
msgid ""
"[Q-VAE for Energy-Supervised Anomaly Detection](qvae_anomaly.md) *Coming "
"soon*: CleanEnergyQVAE with a free-energy scoring head and NCE-style "
"contrastive objective on thyroid / creditcard benchmarks. Example: "
"`example/qvae_anomaly/`."
msgstr ""

